<title>USA: Storm Winnie inland over E.China, weakening - WSC.</title>
<headline>Storm Winnie inland over E.China, weakening - WSC.</headline>
<dateline>LEXINGTON, Mass. 1997-08-19</dateline>
<text>
<p>Typhoon Winnie, now inland over eastern China, has been downgraded to a tropical storm, independent forecaster Weather Services Corp said on Tuesday.</p>
<p>Winnie, which made landfall south of Shanghai near Ningbo, is weakening rapidly over land as it moves to the northwest.</p>
<p>It will dissipate in about 24 hours, but will dump heavy rainfall along its path, leading to flash flooding and mudslides, WSC said.</p>
</text>
